  "body_mappings": [
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        498.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Around Campion, Western Australia, most farmers were First World War veterans, settlers placed by a government scheme on marginal parcels of farmland. They were inexperienced growers, and a quarter had already quit. In 1932, after drought, roughly 20,000 emus swarmed in from arid country in flocks and trampled the wheat crops."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        391.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        490.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "The farmers' plight took a military turn. In desperation, a delegation of ex-soldiers aired their grievances and asked the Defence Minister for machine-guns. He agreed, sending not a battalion but a detachment: Major Meredith, an artillery officer, with two soldiers, two Lewis guns, and 10,000 rounds of ammunition. The offensive began on 2 November 1932."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        263.8614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        382.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "At a dam, about a thousand birds approached an ambush, but a gun jammed after a dozen fell. The flocks broke formation into small, agile groups, frustrating each tactical plan, and a truck-mounted gun proved futile. Six days of wasteful firing spent 2,500 rounds on perhaps 50 to 200 birds, a ludicrous return. After parliamentary questions and press ridicule, an embarrassing withdrawal came on 8 November, though shooting restarted within days."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        176.16141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        255.3614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Meredith was recalled on 10 December. His memo's inventory counted 986 kills from 9,860 rounds, a ratio of ten bullets to one bird. He likened the resilient birds' toughness to the armour of tanks. Five weeks of warfare had barely dented the hardy flocks' endurance."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        88.46141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        167.66141732283472
      ],
      "text": "Later pleas for reinforcements were refused, and intervention gave way to a bounty sanctioned by the government. This payout per bird gave farmers compensation and an incentive for extermination. Farmers claimed over 57,000 payments in six months of 1934, more than fifty-seven times Meredith's 986 kills."
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        517.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "在西澳大利亚州坎皮恩一带，大多数农民是第一次世界大战的退伍军人，他们作为定居者，由政府计划安置在贫瘠的/边缘的小块土地上，以这些农地为生。他们是缺乏经验的种植者，已有四分之一的人放弃了土地。1932年，旱灾过后，约2万只鸸鹋成群地从干旱地区蜂拥而至，践踏了（指动物破坏）小麦庄稼。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        429.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "农民的困境由此走向了军事手段。绝望之中，一个由退伍士兵组成的代表团公开表达了他们的不满/委屈，请求国防部长提供机枪。部长同意了，但派出的不是一个营，而是一支小分队：梅雷迪思少校，一名炮兵军官，带着两名士兵、两挺刘易斯机枪和1万发弹药。进攻于1932年11月2日展开。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        300.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        420.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "在一处水坝，约一千只鸟靠近了埋伏/伏击范围，但打倒十来只后，一挺机枪就卡壳了。鸟群打乱了（它们自己的）队形，（它们）分成了灵活的小群体，挫败了每一个战术计划；装在卡车上的机枪也徒劳无功。六天的浪费的射击花费了/消耗了2,500发，只打死大约50至200只鸟，这是一个荒唐可笑的回报。在议会质询和报界嘲笑/嘲讽之后，一场尴尬的撤退发生在11月8日；不过没过几天，射击又重新开始了。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        232.16141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        292.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "梅雷迪思于12月10日被召回。他在备忘录里开列的清单计数（显示），9,860发打死了986只，比例是十发子弹对一只鸟。他把这些耐打的鸟的坚韧比作坦克的装甲。五个星期的战事几乎没有削弱这些顽强的鸟群的耐受力/抗造力。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        143.66141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        223.66141732283472
      ],
      "text": "后来请求增援的恳求都遭到拒绝，干预转变为（让步于）政府批准的悬赏。这种按只计算的钱款支出（赏金）给了农民补偿，也成为彻底消灭鸸鹋的激励。农民在1934年的六个月里领取了5.7万多笔（赏金）支付，是梅雷迪思那986只战果的五十七倍多。"
    }
  ],
